      "id": 1,
      "text": "Founded in 1925 as a resort for middle‑class African Americans, Eagle Harbor incorporated in 1929.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17,
        18,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eagle_Harbor%2C_Maryland",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Originally called Trueman Point, the town began as a tobacco shipping port in the early 1700s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eagle_Harbor%2C_Maryland",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Eagle Harbor sits on the Patuxent River and is a designated Historical Black Site by the National Heritage Area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.townofeagleharborincmd.org/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The 1927 Eagle Harbor Citizens Association celebrated its 100‑year anniversary in 2027, marking a century of community life.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10,
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://ehcamd.org/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Chalk Point Generating Station borders Eagle Harbor and was sold to Mirant in 2000.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
